<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese escudo rock steady after rate cut.</title>
<headline>Portuguese escudo rock steady after rate cut.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The escudo showed no reaction to the Bank of Portugal's surprise decision on Friday to cut its repurchase pact rate by 30 basis points to 6.0 percent.</p>
<p>The currency was trading at 100.60 to the mark after the announcement, unchanged on earlier levels.</p>
<p>&quot;Mark-escudo was calm and that was how it remained after the announcement, without any reaction,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
